; PARSE-3: with no `commodity` directive and no `decimal-mark`, hledger infers
; each literal's own decimal mark. A single separator is the decimal point
; regardless of how many digits follow it, so `1,50` is one-and-a-half and
; `$1,234` is one-point-two-three-four. A distinct commodity per case keeps
; each literal's inferred style independent.
2017-01-01
    a    1,50 CHF
    b   -1,50 CHF

2017-01-02
    a    $1,234
    b   -$1,234

2017-01-03
    a    1.234,56 SEK
    b   -1.234,56 SEK
